# Binary artifacts: never line-ending-convert, never diff as text.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The vendored TFG checkpoints under
# audit/fa_fb_search/TFG/ are 28 MB of weights that our transfer experiment
# loads directly. Without an explicit rule git classifies them as
# "unspecified" and falls back to a content heuristic, and the team works
# across Windows, Linux and the Betty cluster -- exactly the setup where
# core.autocrlf differs between clones. A checkpoint that got CRLF-converted
# would still load and would still produce molecules; it would just produce
# wrong ones, with nothing raising. That is the failure mode this project
# keeps finding the hard way, so the classification is stated rather than
# inferred.

*.npy      binary
*.pt       binary
*.pth      binary
*.pickle   binary
*.pkl      binary
*.tar.gz   binary
*.tgz      binary
*.zip      binary
*.sdf      binary
*.pdf      binary

# Source and text: normalise to LF in the repository, check out native.
*.py       text diff=python
*.md       text
*.json     text
*.yaml     text
*.yml      text
*.txt      text
*.csv      text

# Shell and SLURM scripts must keep LF even on a Windows checkout -- a CRLF
# shebang line makes the cluster's interpreter fail with a confusing
# "bad interpreter: No such file or directory".
*.sh       text eol=lf
*.slurm    text eol=lf
